          %p
            Such a pseudonatural transformation is called a
            %strong pseudonatural equivalence
            if each component
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta(x)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            in the 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒴
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{Y}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            itself being an equivalence in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor+2-category"} 2-functor 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒴
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{X},\mathcal{Y}]
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"} modifications
            between those.
